(
========================================================================
 PUZZLESCRIPT+ EXTENSIONS TUTORIAL - MESSAGING & FLOW
 This is NOT vanilla PuzzleScript. Paste it into the PuzzleScript+
 editor (Auroriax/PuzzleScriptPlus on GitHub, hosted from that repo's
 gh-pages site) - it will NOT compile at puzzlescript.net, since every
 feature below is a PS+-only addition on top of the base engine.

 Read puzzlescript_tutorial_4_messaging.pss (in this same repo) FIRST.
 Everything from that file - MESSAGE, the in-rule "message" command,
 CHECKPOINT, RESTART, CANCEL, WIN, noundo, norestart - still works
 completely unchanged here. This file covers ONLY what PS+ adds on
 top of that, checked against Auroriax/PuzzleScriptPlus's own engine
 source, not guessed from memory.

 TUTORIAL MAP -- Ctrl+F for a tag like [T3] to jump straight to it.

 [T1] level_select + section + both forms of "goto" - jump straight
      to any section from an in-game menu, or redirect the player
      there from a rule or from the LEVELS list itself
 [T2] level_select_lock, level_select_unlocked_ahead, and
      level_select_solve_symbol - locking the menu until earlier
      sections are solved, plus continue_is_level_select
 [T3] runtime_metadata_twiddling: a RULE changing noundo/norestart
      live, mid-game - this is PS+'s real answer to "overwrite undo
      or restart," well beyond the static Prelude-only vanilla switch
 [T4] Three more in-RULE commands vanilla doesn't have at all: undo
      (trigger a real undo from a rule), nosave (this turn doesn't go
      on the undo stack), and quit (bail to the menu or title screen)
 [T5] message_text_align / text_message_continue / text_controls -
      you've been looking at all three since this file's first
      screen; see the note here for why
 [T6] grab bag: nokeyboard, sprite_size, case_sensitive, tween_*

 Reload this file (hit RUN again) after the first compile: because of
 skip_title_screen plus continue_is_level_select below, you'll land
 straight in the level-select menu instead of a title screen - and
 that menu IS this tutorial's table of contents, one entry per section
 tag above.
========================================================================
)

title PuzzleScript+ Extensions - Messaging & Flow Tutorial
author Claude, for Gail

( [T1] -- lets the player open an in-game menu and jump straight to   )
( any SECTION below, instead of only ever advancing linearly.         )
level_select

( [T2] -- lock sections until nearby progress unlocks them.           )
level_select_lock
level_select_unlocked_ahead 2
level_select_solve_symbol done
continue_is_level_select
skip_title_screen

( [T3] -- required before any rule below is allowed to change a       )
( "twiddleable" flag like noundo/norestart at runtime. Compiles to an )
( error without this line - try deleting it and reloading if you want )
( to see that error for yourself.                                     )
runtime_metadata_twiddling

( [T5] -- global for the whole file, same as noundo/norestart back in )
( the vanilla tutorial. You've already seen these three in effect on  )
( every screen so far; see [T5] below for what to look for. )
message_text_align left
text_message_continue Tap X, boss.
text_controls Arrows to move, X for everything else.

