LEVELS
========================================================================

section LevelSelect

#########
#P......#
#......d#
#########
MESSAGE [T1]: press Escape (or however your build exposes it) to open the level-select menu at any point from here on - every SECTION line below becomes one entry in it. Sections, not individual levels, are the unit level_select jumps between.

MESSAGE [T1] continued - one more form of "goto" before we move on: the LEVELS list itself can hold a standalone "goto SomeSection" line, unconditionally redirecting the player there the moment it's reached in sequence - same mechanism a rule's own "goto" command uses, just triggered by reaching this point in the LEVELS list rather than by anything the player did.

goto Locking

section Locking

#########
#P......#
#......d#
#########
MESSAGE [T2]: level_select_lock greys out sections you haven't reached yet, except for a short lookahead - level_select_unlocked_ahead 2 keeps roughly the next couple visible so you're not staring at a wall of locked entries.

MESSAGE [T2] continued: solve a section (reach its Exit) and level_select_solve_symbol's text marks it done in the menu. continue_is_level_select means "continue" on the title screen opens this same menu, not just a resume - moot here since skip_title_screen skips that screen outright.

section TwiddleUndo

#############
#P..s....u..#
#...........#
#..........d#
#############
MESSAGE [T3]: touching Seal disabled undo AND restart at once - two separate rules, both matching Seal, each contributing one twiddle command to the same turn. Touching Unseal wiped both flags again.

MESSAGE [T3] continued: try Z and R directly - they really do stop responding after Seal, and work again after Unseal, all without touching the Prelude or reloading. That's the part static noundo/norestart back in the vanilla file couldn't do.

section UndoNosaveQuit

###############
#P.r....b...m.#
#.............#
#............d#
###############
MESSAGE [T4]: RewindTile silently undid your last step - no popup, on purpose: firing "undo" clears any pending message that same turn before the undo happens, so combining undo with message on one rule would just show nothing at all.

MESSAGE [T4] continued: crossing the Bridge turned it to Water and popped a message, but notice Z now refuses to rebuild that bridge - nosave kept that turn off the undo stack entirely. MenuButton's "quit" dropped you back at the [T1] level-select menu, not the level's own start.

section MessageStyle

#########
#P......#
#......d#
#########
MESSAGE [T5]: every message screen in this file, including this one, has been left-aligned instead of centered, and the button hint at the bottom read your own custom text instead of the default "X to continue."

MESSAGE [T5] continued: that's message_text_align, text_message_continue, and text_controls - all three set once in the Prelude, applying globally, the same "declare it once, it affects everything" pattern noundo/norestart used back in the vanilla tutorial.

section GrabBag

MESSAGE [T6] grab bag, part 1: nokeyboard drops the Player/movement requirement entirely, for mouse-only games - it would break every level in this file, so it's only described here, not turned on. sprite_size lets object art be something other than the fixed 5x5 grid every sprite in this repo has used so far.

MESSAGE [T6] grab bag, part 2: case_sensitive makes LEGEND symbols distinguish uppercase from lowercase - off by default, same as vanilla, which is why every object here still got its own visually distinct symbol rather than leaning on case.

MESSAGE [T6] grab bag, part 3: tween_length / tween_easing / tween_snap smoothly animate movement between cells instead of vanilla's instant snap - nice polish, but unrelated to messaging or undo/restart, so it only gets a mention here.

MESSAGE That's everything PS+ adds on top of the vanilla file for messaging and flow. One more of these lives in this repo for PuzzleScript Next specifically - go compare what it adds on top of PS+.
